WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.489
Question eleven.

00:00:01.489 --> 00:00:07.537
Step one: macro scan. It asks decimal forty-three in hexadecimal.

00:00:07.537 --> 00:00:11.072
One mark. Command words: “convert to”.

00:00:11.072 --> 00:00:12.747
Step two: denoise.

00:00:12.747 --> 00:00:15.632
Useful, in yellow: forty-three.

00:00:15.632 --> 00:00:18.981
In cyan: “decimal” to “hexadecimal”.

00:00:18.981 --> 00:00:23.634
Useless red herring: sensor reading — kick it out.

00:00:23.634 --> 00:00:25.308
Step three: draft.

00:00:25.308 --> 00:00:30.333
Forty-three divided by sixteen: two, remainder eleven.

00:00:30.333 --> 00:00:32.194
Eleven is written B.

00:00:32.194 --> 00:00:33.682
Together: two B.

00:00:33.682 --> 00:00:35.264
Step four: P O E.

00:00:35.264 --> 00:00:38.707
A, two five: only thirty-seven — cut.

00:00:38.707 --> 00:00:41.219
C, two D: forty-five — cut.

00:00:41.219 --> 00:00:43.824
D, two F: forty-seven — cut.

00:00:43.824 --> 00:00:52.664
Step five: sanity check and lock. Two times sixteen plus eleven equals forty-three. Checks out.

00:00:52.664 --> 00:00:55.176
So the correct answer is B.
